From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kernel/configs: gts3-android: vkms for a board without a
 panel

A Tab S3 whose display is off the board (a developer's, or one being
repaired) has no connected panel, so neither the recovery's GUI nor
Android's SurfaceFlinger finds a display. Both already ask for the
virtual KMS driver when gts3.vkms=1 is on the command line; the module
has to exist for that. It is never loaded otherwise.

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel/configs/gts3-android.config | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/configs/gts3-android.config b/kernel/configs/gts3-android.config
index a8f2b07..8d18122 100644
--- a/kernel/configs/gts3-android.config
+++ b/kernel/configs/gts3-android.config
@@ -126,3 +126,7 @@ CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS=y
 CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS_SYSTEM=y
 CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS_CMA=y
 CONFIG_INPUT_EGIS_ET5XX_CTRL=m
+
+# A virtual display, for a board whose panel is not connected: the recovery
+# and gsi-init turn it on with gts3.vkms=1 and draw on card1
+CONFIG_DRM_VKMS=m
